  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Fix potential integer overflow in getnum",
  "description": "`getnum` in `epan/wslua/wslua_struct.c` potentially has an integer overflow if `fmt` is set too large.\nIt might be triggered by running such lua statment: `EVAL \"struct.pack('>I2147483648', '10')\" 0`. It's somehow similiar to [CVE-2020-14147](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2020-14147), so I fix this by adding a bound check in `getnum`, referring to the [patch](https://github.com/redis/redis/commit/ef764dde1cca2f25d00686673d1bc89448819571)",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2024-02-03T04:19:05.334Z",
